30 cases, the same retrieved context for both, two models.

                     correct   refused      p50      p95  out tokens
  gpt-5.4-mini      22/30      7/12        1.0s     1.5s         557
  gpt-5.5           18/30      6/12        1.5s     3.3s       2,007

  (no rates set, so this table reports tokens and stays silent about
   dollars — Appendix C says where to find current prices)

This is the table the gateway exists to make possible, and it is worth being
precise about what it does and does not say.

It says these two models score 22/30 and 18/30 on this suite, at these
latencies, for these token counts. That is a fact about Meridian's questions
and Meridian's documents, measured on a Tuesday.

It does not say which model is better. Nothing does. There is no such number,
and the published leaderboards answer a question nobody in your building is
asking — Chapter 21 spent forty pages on why your own cases are the only ones
that transfer.

Two things to check before trusting any row of this table:

  the context was held fixed   both models saw identical passages, fetched
                               once. Re-running retrieval per model measures
                               retrieval variance and calls it a model
                               difference
  the interval is wide         §21.6's arithmetic applies here unchanged; on
                               thirty cases a two-point gap is nothing

And a provider comparison is not only a quality comparison. Chapter 27's last
section is about the fact that compliance, data residency and contractual
terms routinely decide this before capability gets a vote — and they are much
harder to change later than a model name in a config file.
